Prevent continuously writable descriptors from spinning the Solaris selector.

Fallback interests must not remain associated with the event port at the same
time. Otherwise a writable socket makes port_getn return immediately and the
zero-timeout fallback poll reports the same readiness again, bypassing the
intended ten millisecond bound.

Track whether fallback interests are still associated, restore drained
directions independently, and report continuous writable readiness only once.
This preserves the fallback needed for missed event-port edges without keeping
Tokio and Reqwest runtimes permanently runnable.

